  "requirement": "Before that commit, the `habeas-requirements` skill MUST direct agents to check that the book holds exactly the agreed text.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The requirement has one obligation. Before the commit, the `habeas-requirements` skill must direct agents to check that the book holds exactly the agreed text. The text names no other modes, boundaries or failure cases.\n\n`tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[the_requirements_skill_checks_the_book_holds_exactly_the_agreed_text]` is marked `{test}` for the subject. It calls `assert_phrases(\"habeas-requirements\", ...)`, which runs `assert_text` on `bundled_skill`. `bundled_skill` joins `SKILL.md` and its reference files and collapses whitespace. `assert_text` asserts that the text contains \"Check with `git diff` that the book holds exactly the agreed text, then commit it\". It panics if the phrase is missing.\n\nThe phrase covers both parts of the obligation. It directs a check that the book holds exactly the agreed text. \"Then commit it\" puts that check before the commit.\n\nThe skill's step 5 (Commit) in `assets/skills/habeas-requirements/SKILL.md` contains the sentence, wrapped across lines. The whitespace collapse makes the match work. If the directive were removed or reworded, the assertion would fail. I found no scenario that violates the requirement and still passes this test, and no marking gap.",
